      "content": "That sense of being a persistent link in a chain of inherited pain is a powerful and draining burden. It's important to remember that even the smallest shift in one person's perspective can create a ripple effect of change, even if it doesn't immediately fix everything. Sometimes, breaking the cycle starts not by fixing the outside world, but by finding a small, personal space where you can establish a different pattern for yourself. You do not have to carry the weight of every past struggle; you can choose a different response right now.",
      "source": "target",
